// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeKeepWritesMadeOffline(path: "/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline", title: "Keep writes made offline — Recipes", description: "Keep the reader's changes when the network drops: with sync on, a write that fails offline is kept and sent in order when the connection returns.") {
    RecipeShell("Keep writes made offline", summary: "Keep the reader's changes when the network drops, and send them when it comes back. This needs offline support turned on ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)), with `\"sync\": true` in its config:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Translate a site", to: "/recipes/translate-a-site"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Translate by the words as written", to: "/recipes/translate-by-the-words"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Publish a page in each language", to: "/recipes/site-in-two-languages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/keep-writes-made-offline.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** `offline` with `\"sync\": true` in `webfluent.app.json`, below, and a site served over HTTPS ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline)).")
            CodeBlock(#"{ "offline": { "precache": ["/"], "sync": true } }"#, title: "json")
            Markdown("This page tells the reader how many changes are waiting to be sent:")
            CodeBlock(#"page Notes(path: "/notes", title: "Notes", description: "Notes that save offline.") {
    Heading("Notes").h1
    if network.queued > 0 {
        Text("{network.queued} change(s) will be sent when you are back online").muted
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("With `sync` on, a write — any method but `GET` and `HEAD`, made through `fetch` or an `api` — that fails because the network is gone is kept instead of thrown. The call resolves with nothing, so what the page showed stays shown.\n\n`network.queued` is how many writes are waiting. Show it, as the page above does, so the reader knows their changes are safe.")

        Heading("What is kept", id: "what-is-kept").h3

        Markdown("Only a write that failed for want of a network is kept: the browser says it is offline, or the site's own server could not be reached. A request to another origin that is refused while the browser is online — a CORS refusal, a closed port — fails as it would without `sync`.\n\nA credential is never stored with a kept write. What an `api`'s `on request` hook adds — an `Authorization` header from the session — is added again when the write is sent, by the hook as it is then: a write made before a logout goes out with no one's token, never the old one. A write whose call carries a credential header itself (`headers: \{ \"Authorization\": token \}`) cannot be kept without it, so it is not kept, and its call fails as it would without `sync`.\n\nA `File` body is not kept, and its call fails as it would without `sync`.")

        Heading("When it is sent", id: "when-it-is-sent").h3

        Markdown("When the connection returns, the kept writes are sent in order:\n\n- by Background Sync, where the browser has it, so a closed tab still sends them;\n- by the page otherwise, the next time it is open.\n\nA server that answers has the write, even if it refuses it. A server that is down, or asks the client to wait, keeps the write waiting for later.\n\nA write whose service adds credentials with its hook is sent by a page that has that service open, so the worker leaves it — and the writes after it, to keep them in order — for the next such page.")

        Heading("Forget the kept writes", id: "forget-the-kept-writes").h3

        Markdown("To forget every kept write — when the reader logs out, for example — call `WF.clearQueued()` from one of the project's scripts.")

    }
}
